---
import Section from './Section.astro';
// Two ways to run it + the data-custody promise. Honesty: the mobile app is
// Phase 2, so the hosted plan "opens with the app" — no sign-up now, matching
// the status ribbon. Every security claim is limited to what the repo verifiably
// does (README self-hosting guide + docs/MULTI_USER.md §3.3): row-level security
// + least-privilege role, Supabase-owned passwords, internet-closed DB + TLS,
// nightly off-box pg_dump. No encryption-at-rest / audit / compliance claims.
const promise = [
  {
    t: 'Isolated by the database itself',
    d: 'Every row of your data is tied to your account, and the database enforces that line — so one account can never read another’s, even if our code makes a mistake.',
  },
  {
    t: 'We never see your password',
    d: 'Sign-in is handled by Supabase. Your password never reaches our server, and we never store it.',
  },
  {
    t: 'Never open to the internet',
    d: 'The database sits behind the wall, reachable only by the app itself; everything in transit is encrypted with TLS.',
  },
  {
    t: 'Backed up nightly, off the box',
    d: 'A nightly backup is shipped off the server, so a lost machine isn’t lost data.',
  },
  {
    t: 'Yours, with no lock-in',
    d: 'No trackers, no analytics, and we never sell your data. Self-host and the whole database is already yours.',
  },
];
---

<Section id="self-host" tone="sunk" labelledby="selfhost-h">
  <h2 id="selfhost-h" class="rise mt-4 max-w-2xl text-[clamp(1.9rem,4vw,3rem)]">
    Run it yourself, or let us run it for you.
  </h2>
  <p class="lede rise mt-6 max-w-2xl">
    The backend is complete, deployed, and multi-tenant. You can host the whole thing yourself today
    — or wait for the hosted version that arrives with the app.
  </p>

  <div class="mt-10 grid gap-6 lg:grid-cols-2">
    <!-- self-host -->
    <div class="surface rise flex flex-col p-7 sm:p-8">
      <div class="flex items-center justify-between gap-3">
        <h3 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Self-host it</h3>
        <span class="chip chip-accent chip-dot">free, yours forever</span>
      </div>
      <p class="mt-4 text-[0.95rem] leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
        Your server, your database, your data — nothing ever leaves your box. Healthee runs on one
        small VPS, and the whole thing is yours to change.
      </p>
      <ul class="mt-5 space-y-2.5 text-[0.92rem] text-ink-soft">
        <li class="flex gap-3"><span aria-hidden="true" class="mono shrink-0 text-accent-soft">✓</span> Runs on a single small server you control</li>
        <li class="flex gap-3"><span aria-hidden="true" class="mono shrink-0 text-accent-soft">✓</span> Database never touches the internet</li>
        <li class="flex gap-3"><span aria-hidden="true" class="mono shrink-0 text-accent-soft">✓</span> Nightly off-box backup in one command</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="mono mt-6 text-xs text-ink-faint">For the technically inclined.</p>
    </div>

    <!-- hosted -->
    <div class="surface rise flex flex-col p-7 sm:p-8">
      <div class="flex items-center justify-between gap-3">
        <h3 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Let us host it</h3>
        <span class="chip chip-dot">opens with the app</span>
      </div>
      <p class="mt-4 text-[0.95rem] leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
        Don’t want to run a server? We’ll run the same code for you — the same honesty, none of the
        setup. Tracking stays free; you’d pay only for the AI layer, exactly as priced above.
      </p>
      <ul class="mt-5 space-y-2.5 text-[0.92rem] text-ink-soft">
        <li class="flex gap-3"><span aria-hidden="true" class="mono shrink-0 text-accent-soft">✓</span> Same app, same guarantees, zero setup</li>
        <li class="flex gap-3"><span aria-hidden="true" class="mono shrink-0 text-accent-soft">✓</span> You sign in; we handle the rest</li>
        <li class="flex gap-3"><span aria-hidden="true" class="mono shrink-0 text-accent-soft">✓</span> Your data still isolated and yours</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="mt-6 border-t border-line pt-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-faint">
        Sign-ups open when the app ships (Phase 2). They’re closed today — no waitlist, no pretending.
        Follow the build, and this is where they’ll open.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- where the code lives -->
  <p class="rise mt-6 max-w-3xl text-[0.95rem] leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
    The whole thing runs on one small server you control. The code goes up on GitHub the
    moment it&rsquo;s ready to run yourself &mdash; and the link will appear right here.
    <span class="text-ink-faint">Still being built, out in the open. No link yet, no
    pretending otherwise.</span>
  </p>

  <!-- the custody promise -->
  <div class="rise mt-14 max-w-3xl">
    <h3 class="mt-4 text-[clamp(1.5rem,3vw,2.1rem)] font-semibold tracking-tight">
      The promise covers your data, not just our words.
    </h3>
    <dl class="mt-8 grid gap-x-10 gap-y-6 sm:grid-cols-2">
      {
        promise.map((p) => (
          <div>
            <dt class="flex items-center gap-2.5 font-medium">
              <span aria-hidden="true" class="inline-block h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-accent"></span>
              {p.t}
            </dt>
            <dd class="mt-1.5 text-[0.92rem] leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">{p.d}</dd>
          </div>
        ))
      }
    </dl>
    <p class="mono mt-8 text-xs leading-relaxed text-ink-faint">
      In plain terms above. By its technical name, that database-level isolation is row-level security
      enforced through a least-privilege connection. We don’t claim more than the code does — no
      encryption-at-rest, audits, or compliance badges here, because the repo doesn’t show them.
    </p>
  </div>
</Section>
